If $\mathop{\mathrm{Val}}(\mathcal G)\ge1-a$, the graph has a cut of value at least $$\label{eq:completeness}
 (1-2Ta)\frac{1+t r^{2d}}2
 \ge\frac{1+t}{2}-t\mu-2Ta.$$ The first lower bound is useful when $2Ta\le1$, which is the regime used below.

For every fixed $\underline y$, $\mathcal D$, $v$, $\Gamma$, $F_{\mathrm{out}}$, and label $q\in\mathcal A$, $$\label{eq:unsmooth}
 m_q(\bar G_{\underline y};\Gamma,F_{\mathrm{out}})
 \leq
 \mathbb E_{E,\,\underline e\mid\underline y}
 m_q(G_{\underline e};\Gamma+E_\Gamma,F_{\mathrm{out}}).$$ Here the noise $E$ is independent of the conditionally sampled edge tuple $\underline e$.

evidence.quote:
Fix $t\in(0,1)$, $0<\delta<1-B(t)$, and $0<\mu<1/2$. There are tree parameters $s\ge2,m\ge1$ and constants $p_*,\theta>0$, depending only on $t,\delta,\mu$, with the following property. For any affine label space $\mathcal A$ and any family $\phi_\omega$ as above, if $$\label{eq:excess-stability}
 \mathbb E_{\omega,\mathcal D,R,F_{\mathrm{out}}}
 \mathop{\mathrm{Stab}}_t^{F_{\mathcal D}}(\bar f_\omega)
 \ge B(t)+\delta,$$ then $$\label{eq:extraction-event}
 \Pr\left[
   \max_{q\in\mathcal A}
   m_q(\bar f_\omega;\Gamma,F_{\mathrm{out}})\ge\theta
 \right]\ge p_*.$$ Here we sample $\omega$, the random slice $\mathcal D$, and a uniform node $v\in\mathcal D$; conditional on these, we sample $F_{\mathrm{out}}$ and $\Gamma$ independently and uniformly.

outputs.exact_statement:
If $\mathop{\mathrm{Val}}(\mathcal G)\ge1-a$, the graph has a cut of value at least $$\label{eq:completeness}
 (1-2Ta)\frac{1+t r^{2d}}2
 \ge\frac{1+t}{2}-t\mu-2Ta.$$ The first lower bound is useful when $2Ta\le1$, which is the regime used below.

For every cut of the constructed graph, $$\label{eq:cut-stability}
 \operatorname{cut}(\sigma)=\frac12+
 \frac12\mathbb E\mathop{\mathrm{Stab}}_t^{F_{\mathcal D}}(\bar G_{\underline y})
 -\frac12\mathbb E\mathop{\mathrm{Stab}}_t^{F_{\mathcal D}}(\bar A_{\underline y}),$$ where both expectations are over $\underline y,\mathcal D,R,F_{\mathrm{out}}$. In particular, $$\label{eq:cut-upper-stability}
 \operatorname{cut}(\sigma)\le\frac12+
 \frac12\mathbb E\mathop{\mathrm{Stab}}_t^{F_{\mathcal D}}(\bar G_{\underline y}).$$

Let $f$ be a function of the code with $|f|\le1$, let $r=1-\mu/d$ with $0<\mu<1/2$, and let $\bar f=T_rf$. Choose the random slice independently of $f$. Then $$\mathbb E_{J_0,\mathcal D}\sum_{v\in\mathcal D}
       \norm{(I-S_v)\bar f}_{2,R,F}^{2}
       \le \frac{s}{2e m\mu}.
 \label{eq:unsplit-bound}$$ The same bound holds after averaging over additional background data determining $f$, provided the slice is chosen independently of those data.

Fix $t\in(0,1)$, $0<\delta<1-B(t)$, and $0<\mu<1/2$. There are tree parameters $s\ge2,m\ge1$ and constants $p_*,\theta>0$, depending only on $t,\delta,\mu$, with the following property. For any affine label space $\mathcal A$ and any family $\phi_\omega$ as above, if $$\label{eq:excess-stability}
 \mathbb E_{\omega,\mathcal D,R,F_{\mathrm{out}}}
 \mathop{\mathrm{Stab}}_t^{F_{\mathcal D}}(\bar f_\omega)
 \ge B(t)+\delta,$$ then $$\label{eq:extraction-event}
 \Pr\left[
   \max_{q\in\mathcal A}
   m_q(\bar f_\omega;\Gamma,F_{\mathrm{out}})\ge\theta
 \right]\ge p_*.$$ Here we sample $\omega$, the random slice $\mathcal D$, and a uniform node $v\in\mathcal D$; conditional on these, we sample $F_{\mathrm{out}}$ and $\Gamma$ independently and uniformly.

For every fixed $\underline y$, $\mathcal D$, $v$, $\Gamma$, $F_{\mathrm{out}}$, and label $q\in\mathcal A$, $$\label{eq:unsmooth}
 m_q(\bar G_{\underline y};\Gamma,F_{\mathrm{out}})
 \leq
 \mathbb E_{E,\,\underline e\mid\underline y}
 m_q(G_{\underline e};\Gamma+E_\Gamma,F_{\mathrm{out}}).$$ Here the noise $E$ is independent of the conditionally sampled edge tuple $\underline e$.

Let $\mathsf U$ be the unplanted law and $\mathsf P$ the planted law after forgetting the mark. Both laws are taken on the full data $$\bigl(\underline e,J_0,\mathcal D,v,F_{\mathrm{out}},
        \Gamma,R^{\mathrm{new}},B\bigr).$$ Then $$\label{eq:planting-tv}
 \mathop{\mathrm{TV}}(\mathsf P,\mathsf U)
 \leq \frac12\sqrt{\frac{1-p_0}{Tp_0}}
 \leq \frac{1}{2\sqrt{Tp_0}}.$$ Consequently, if $$\label{eq:decoder-repetition}
 T\geq\frac{1}{p_0(p_*\theta)^2},$$ then under the planted law, $$\label{eq:planted-score}
 \mathbb E_{\mathsf P}\,m_{q^*}(G_{\underline e};
               \Gamma+E_\Gamma,F_{\mathrm{out}})
 \geq \frac{p_*\theta}{2}.$$

Fix a context and the outside tables. Let $\widetilde f(\widetilde L,F_{\mathcal D})$ be a function on $\widetilde H^{2s}$ and the slice tables. Suppose its shift Fourier support has the common-pair-sum property $$\widetilde Q_{g0}+\widetilde Q_{g1}
 =\widetilde Q_{h0}+\widetilde Q_{h1}
 \quad\text{for all }g,h\in[s].$$ Set $f(L,F_{\mathcal D})=
\widetilde f(\iota L,F_{\mathcal D})$, where $\iota$ acts on each shift. For every label $q\in\mathcal A$, $$\label{eq:restriction-mass}
 m_q(f)\leq 2^{2s}
       \sum_{\substack{\widetilde q\in\widetilde{\mathcal A}\\
                       \rho(\widetilde q)=q}}
          \widetilde m_{\widetilde q}(\widetilde f).$$ The masses on both sides use the common-pair-sum definition of Equation <a href="#eq:mass" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:mass">[eq:mass]</a>, with the respective affine row spaces.
